.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH swarm 1  "swarm 0.2.1" "Swarmgit manual"
.SH NAME
swarm \- Zero\-setup peer\-to\-peer git
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswarm\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Swarmgit is a peer\-to\-peer git remote. A repository has a swarm:// link, and anyone who can reach a peer holding it can clone it, with no server and no account. You keep using git; the git\-remote\-swarm helper handles swarm:// remotes, and a background daemon talks to peers. Pushing needs the repository\*(Aqs root or maintainer key, while anyone with the link can open and discuss merge requests.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
swarm\-init(1)
Create a repo key and publish the first manifest
.TP
swarm\-link(1)
Print the link for a repo
.TP
swarm\-status(1)
Show the daemon, repos, relays and peers
.TP
swarm\-inspect(1)
Show a repo\*(Aqs name, branches and forks without downloading Git objects
.TP
swarm\-about(1)
Show or set a repo\*(Aqs name and description (root or maintainer key)
.TP
swarm\-discover\-relays(1)
Find public relay servers through the Mainline DHT and relay gossip
.TP
swarm\-seed(1)
Sync a repo and keep serving it
.TP
swarm\-unseed(1)
Stop serving a repo but keep its store
.TP
swarm\-gc(1)
Repack a repo\*(Aqs store and drop unreachable objects, when idle (ST\-7)
.TP
swarm\-purge(1)
Delete a repo\*(Aqs store and manifests, and stop serving it
.TP
swarm\-mr(1)
Merge requests: propose changes, discuss, review and merge them
.TP
swarm\-fork(1)
Create an independent repo from another one
.TP
swarm\-export(1)
Write a repo and its signed state to a bundle file for offline transfer
.TP
swarm\-mirror(1)
Publish a repo for static mirrors (plain file hosting)
.TP
swarm\-import(1)
Read a bundle file, making its repo available offline
.TP
swarm\-maintainers(1)
Add or remove maintainers, who may publish without the root key
.TP
swarm\-accept(1)
Settle a ref conflict here by taking one signer\*(Aqs value
.TP
swarm\-key(1)
Key management
.TP
swarm\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script (bash, zsh, fish, elvish, powershell)
.TP
swarm\-relay(1)
Run a relay server for peers that cannot accept connections
.TP
swarm\-daemon(1)
Start, stop or restart the background daemon
.SH VERSION
v0.2.1
.SH EXAMPLES
Publish the repository you are in, then clone it elsewhere with its link:
.PP
.nf
swarm init
git push swarm main
git clone \(aqswarm://...\(aq
.fi
.PP
Propose a branch for someone else\(aqs repository, from a clone of it:
.PP
.nf
git checkout \-b fix
git commit \-am "Fix the thing"
swarm mr create
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
SWARM_HOME
Where keys, repositories and the daemon\(aqs files are kept.
.TP
SWARM_CONFIG
The configuration file to read.
.SH FILES
.TP
/etc/swarmgit/config.yaml, ~/.config/swarmgit/config.yaml
Settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1).
Each command has its own page, such as
.BR swarm\-mr (1).
The user guide is at https://swarmgit.com/docs.
